<article class="env-remark" id="0G9D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G9D">Remark <span data-tag="0G9D">15.86.2</span>.</a> The following two statements follow from Lemma <a href="/tag/0G9C" data-tag="0G9C">15.86.1</a>, Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/00T2" data-tag="00T2">10.137.1</a>, and Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/031J" data-tag="031J">10.138.8</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A ring map $A \to B$ is smooth if and only if $A \to B$ is of finite presentation and $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ B(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}, N) = 0$ for every $B$-module $N$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A ring map $A \to B$ is formally smooth if and only if $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ B(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}, N) = 0$ for every $B$-module $N$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>